  "configuration_id": "config_033",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_004 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) achieved 71.3% accuracy / 69.5% F1, establishing a working multimodal baseline. Uncertainty: it is unclear whether the relatively modest ResNet50 image encoder is a bottleneck compared to the more powerful ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L. This experiment (config_033) makes a single clean change—swapping image_encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l—while holding the RNA encoder (scvi_n200), aggregation (transformer), fusion (weighted), and profile setting (multiprofile) constant. This directly tests whether a stronger visual backbone translates into higher validation accuracy within the same architectural framework. It is the best use of experiment 2 because: (1) it is a minimal, interpretable ablation that isolates one high-impact variable, (2) if ViT-L helps, it unlocks a family of promising configs (017, 042, 051, etc.) for the remaining 8 experiments, and (3) with only one prior data point, a targeted exploitation of the proven architecture is more informative than a broad exploration or a baseline that would not change the multimodal search trajectory."
}

